# PLAN-1081 — AV 命名函数值与闭包（语言共享语料 functions 面）

The canonical author of the named-function-value / closure language
family. Every case carries ONE Auto source; the `av` check runs the
ordinary AV language chain (`ac-av/language-source-run-v1`); the legacy
`VM result` checks keep their original oracles and owners with the
AV-phase `#ignore` marker (AV-ONLY-1078-1096) — not executed in this
phase, never blocking the AV gate; their backend tasks remove the marker
when they land.

Auditable normalizations (recorded in `language/migration/legacy-map.tsv`,
same policy as PLAN-1080's `double`→`twice`):
- `double` is a reserved numeric type word in the current language — the
  canonical spelling is `twice` (legacy.27_function_reference ×3 and the
  §6 drafts).
- legacy.09_functions.007's untyped lambda params `(a, b) =>` have no
  parameter-inference mechanism on this face — the canonical spelling
  adds `int` annotations (semantics and oracle unchanged).
- legacy.09_functions.010/013's `List.map` HOF algorithm belongs to the
  stdlib/HOF owner (research-hold row); this file carries the
  closure+capture language face through an explicit per-element HOF.

